WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.586
The results are decisive.

00:00:01.666 --> 00:00:06.649
Across every simulated configuration, the Hessian
rule takes the least time,

00:00:06.729 --> 00:00:10.912
and its advantage is largest exactly where
competitors struggle,

00:00:10.992 --> 00:00:13.977
the high-correlation, low-dimensional setting.

00:00:14.057 --> 00:00:17.108
On real data it wins on nearly all twelve sets.

00:00:17.188 --> 00:00:21.039
For ℓ1-regularized least-squares it is fastest on
all five,

00:00:21.119 --> 00:00:26.568
and in all but one case it finishes in under half
the time of the next-best method,

00:00:26.648 --> 00:00:28.234
the working-set strategy.

00:00:28.314 --> 00:00:35.962
On YearPredictionMSD it fits the full path in
seventy-nine seconds against five hundred forty-one for the runner-up,

00:00:36.042 --> 00:00:40.692
and on e2006-tfidf in fourteen seconds against one
hundred forty-three,

00:00:40.772 --> 00:00:43.290
speedups of roughly seven to ten times.
